// How long a block takes to break (pbd_core::dig), in seconds: a matrix of
// one time per digging tool for each class of material. The fastest tool in
// each row is the one that material wants: the shovel for dirt (grass, soil,
// dirt, sand, snow), the pickaxe for stone, rock and ore, the axe for wood.
// A test holds the shipped rows to that. The rod breaks nothing. With the
// button held, the next block starts between_s after the last one broke.
//
// The wood row waits on trees: no material is wood until they can be felled.
//
// The code defaults written out; a test holds the two together. Why these
// numbers, cell by cell: openspec/changes/fishing-and-equipment/design.md
// section 3.
(
    //        shovel        pickaxe        axe
    dirt:   (shovel: 0.5, pickaxe: 1.5, axe: 1.2),
    stone:  (shovel: 4.0, pickaxe: 1.2, axe: 3.0),
    rock:   (shovel: 5.0, pickaxe: 1.6, axe: 4.0),
    ore:    (shovel: 6.5, pickaxe: 2.0, axe: 5.5),
    wood:   (shovel: 2.5, pickaxe: 2.0, axe: 0.6),
    placed: (shovel: 0.1, pickaxe: 0.1, axe: 0.1),
    between_s: 0.15,
)
